2760
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:04,300
My name is Peppa

4794
00:00:04,794 --> 00:00:07,154
And this is my little brother George

7606
00:00:07,606 --> 00:00:08,866
This is Mummy Pig

9878
00:00:09,878 --> 00:00:11,267
This is Daddy Pig

13674
00:00:13,674 --> 00:00:15,045
And I'm Peppa

17035
00:00:17,035 --> 00:00:18,200
[Mysteries]

21375
00:00:21,375 --> 00:00:22,428
Peppa and her family

22479
00:00:22,479 --> 00:00:25,076
are watching their favourite TV show

25127
00:00:25,127 --> 00:00:26,477
"Potato Detective"

26527
00:00:26,527 --> 00:00:28,420
I am Potato Detective

28470
00:00:28,470 --> 00:00:29,965
I'm a world-famous detective

31860
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:33,911
Please help me, Mr Detective

33961
00:00:33,961 --> 00:00:35,901
I can't find my flower anywhere

35952
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:39,442
Well, the flower you're looking for is right on your head

39500
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:41,365
Oh, thank you, Mr Detective

42043
00:00:42,043 --> 00:00:44,880
That's easy, I could've done that

46083
00:00:46,083 --> 00:00:48,153
I'm sure you could

48211
00:00:48,211 --> 00:00:50,023
Daddy, when I grow up

50073
00:00:50,073 --> 00:00:52,313
I want to be a very famous detective

53180
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:54,946
George wants to be a detective too!

55360
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:57,448
If you want to be detectives

57498
00:00:57,498 --> 00:00:59,901
you each need a hat

59952
00:00:59,952 --> 00:01:02,195
Detectives always wear hats, you know

62734
00:01:02,734 --> 00:01:05,735
Now you both look like real detectives

66077
00:01:06,077 --> 00:01:07,996
We also need that funny thing

68046
00:01:08,046 --> 00:01:10,604
that makes everything look bigger

70655
00:01:10,655 --> 00:01:12,590
That's a magnifying glass

72640
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,894
I think there's one in the kitchen drawer

75903
00:01:15,903 --> 00:01:17,165
Here it is

77215
00:01:17,215 --> 00:01:19,391
A real magnifying glass

79442
00:01:19,442 --> 00:01:21,805
Wow, how does it work?

82339
00:01:22,339 --> 00:01:24,372
You hold it in front of something

84422
00:01:24,422 --> 00:01:25,901
and that thing looks bigger

85952
00:01:25,952 --> 00:01:28,645
The magnifying glass made the goldfish look bigger

89472
00:01:29,472 --> 00:01:31,031
Can I try?

92077
00:01:32,077 --> 00:01:33,353
Wow!

93404
00:01:33,404 --> 00:01:36,697
The magnifying glass made George's eye look huge

98303
00:01:38,303 --> 00:01:40,531
Now, what you two detectives need

100581
00:01:40,581 --> 00:01:42,685
is a mystery to solve

102730
00:01:42,730 --> 00:01:45,565
Daddy, what's a... cookie case?

105701
00:01:45,701 --> 00:01:47,263
It's a mystery, not a cookie

107319
00:01:47,319 --> 00:01:50,045
This is what detectives are best at solving

110302
00:01:50,302 --> 00:01:52,405
Like finding things that are lost

112817
00:01:52,817 --> 00:01:53,745
I know!

113795
00:01:53,795 --> 00:01:56,568
We can find George's dinosaur

116676
00:01:56,676 --> 00:01:58,999
He's always losing it

119202
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:00,308
Dinosaur!

120802
00:02:00,802 --> 00:02:02,961
Mr Dinosaur isn't lost

123260
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:06,585
Oh, why don't we find your glasses, Daddy

126636
00:02:06,636 --> 00:02:08,854
You're always saying you can't find them

129758
00:02:09,758 --> 00:02:11,145
They're not lost today!

131195
00:02:11,195 --> 00:02:13,114
My glasses are right here

133165
00:02:13,165 --> 00:02:14,620
Oh no, that's no good

134670
00:02:14,670 --> 00:02:16,954
So there's no cookie mystery for me to solve?

137542
00:02:17,542 --> 00:02:19,853
You want me to make up some mysteries for you to solve?

139904
00:02:19,904 --> 00:02:21,325
Yes please

143302
00:02:23,302 --> 00:02:26,041
Daddy Pig is going to make up some mysteries

146092
00:02:26,092 --> 00:02:28,563
Now, what's on the table?

148613
00:02:28,613 --> 00:02:31,142
There's a little fish, a teddy bear

151193
00:02:31,193 --> 00:02:34,562
a jack-in-the-box, and Mr Dinosaur too

154967
00:02:34,967 --> 00:02:35,805
That's right

156202
00:02:36,202 --> 00:02:37,680
Now watch closely

157736
00:02:37,736 --> 00:02:39,605
Try to remember them

160145
00:02:40,145 --> 00:02:42,269
There's a fish, a teddy bear

162319
00:02:42,319 --> 00:02:44,685
a jack-in-the-box clown, and Mr. Dinosaur

165292
00:02:45,292 --> 00:02:46,743
Have you remembered them all?

166794
00:02:46,794 --> 00:02:48,047
Got them all

168262
00:02:48,262 --> 00:02:49,542
Good

169592
00:02:49,592 --> 00:02:52,298
You two wait outside for a bit

172348
00:02:52,348 --> 00:02:54,548
I'll call you when I'm ready

176294
00:02:56,294 --> 00:02:59,655
That sounds like Daddy going up the stairs

181445
00:03:01,445 --> 00:03:04,186
Now he should be coming back down

184551
00:03:04,551 --> 00:03:07,439
All done, you can come back in now

188399
00:03:08,399 --> 00:03:10,926
Something's gone missing from the table

191093
00:03:11,093 --> 00:03:12,399
Do you know what it is?

192607
00:03:12,607 --> 00:03:14,669
There's Mr. Dinosaur

194719
00:03:14,719 --> 00:03:17,339
the fish, the jack-in-the-box clown

197457
00:03:17,457 --> 00:03:19,253
So who's missing?

199303
00:03:19,303 --> 00:03:21,385
Um... the teddy bear

201436
00:03:21,436 --> 00:03:23,926
That's exactly right, the teddy bear is missing

203977
00:03:23,977 --> 00:03:25,885
Peppa, George, you're so clever!

206289
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:28,233
This is easy for us

208283
00:03:28,283 --> 00:03:30,365
Because we're famous detectives

211257
00:03:31,257 --> 00:03:33,512
But this mystery is only half solved

213562
00:03:33,562 --> 00:03:35,059
Where did the teddy bear go?

215110
00:03:35,110 --> 00:03:36,845
Oh, I don't know

217615
00:03:37,615 --> 00:03:40,048
What are those little bits on the floor?

220512
00:03:40,512 --> 00:03:42,005
Those are cake crumbs

222593
00:03:42,593 --> 00:03:45,725
With a magnifying glass
it's easy to see those are cake crumbs

226526
00:03:46,526 --> 00:03:49,529
I wonder if the teddy bear was eating cake earlier?

229579
00:03:49,579 --> 00:03:52,581
The cake crumbs go this way

233446
00:03:53,446 --> 00:03:56,005
The teddy bear must have eaten a lot of cake

236433
00:03:56,433 --> 00:03:59,241
The cake crumbs lead all the way to Peppa and George's room

239292
00:03:59,292 --> 00:04:01,795
Oh, the crumbs lead here

242064
00:04:02,064 --> 00:04:03,971
How do we find the teddy bear?

244022
00:04:04,022 --> 00:04:05,670
Ask me some questions

245720
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:08,945
But I'll only answer 'yes' or 'no'

248996
00:04:08,996 --> 00:04:10,024
Okay then

251405
00:04:11,405 --> 00:04:13,135
Is the teddy bear in this room?

253193
00:04:13,193 --> 00:04:13,943
Yes

254097
00:04:14,097 --> 00:04:16,273
Is the teddy bear on George's bed?

256324
00:04:16,324 --> 00:04:17,183
No

257234
00:04:17,234 --> 00:04:19,938
Is the teddy bear somewhere high up?

259989
00:04:19,989 --> 00:04:20,740
Yes

262350
00:04:22,350 --> 00:04:23,934
The teddy bear is on my bed

263985
00:04:23,985 --> 00:04:24,805
-Yay!
-Yay!

265306
00:04:25,306 --> 00:04:26,961
Mystery solved!

268974
00:04:28,974 --> 00:04:32,085
Do you want to be a detective when you grow up, Peppa?

272162
00:04:32,162 --> 00:04:35,187
Actually, being a detective isn't easy at all, it's really hard

275237
00:04:35,237 --> 00:04:39,139
Next time, I'd rather be the one who makes up the mysteries

279189
00:04:39,189 --> 00:04:41,298
Just like you, Daddy
